         <span class=\"count\">1</span>\n   443→                </div>\n   444→\n   445→                <div class=\"item\">\n   446→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   447→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Continue</a>\n   448→                    </div>\n   449→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   450→                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span> Added support for Inception Labs' mercury-2 model, expanding the available AI models for code autocomplete and chat features in the IDE extension.\n   451→                    </div>\n   452→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   453→                        <span class=\"meta-item\">📅 April 17, 2026</span>\n   454→                    </div>\n   455→                    <div style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">\n   456→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/commit/cb273098d968906d25ee737b454f0b5f13ea2482\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"highlight-link\">View Commit →</a>\n   457→                    </div>\n   458→                </div>\n   459→            </section>\n   460→\n   461→            <!-- Technical Insights Section (25% width) -->\n   462→            <section class=\"section technical-insights\">\n   463→                <div class=\"section-header\">\n   464→                    Technical Insights\n   465→                    <span class=\"count\">13</span>\n   466→                </div>\n   467→\n   468→                <div class=\"item\">\n   469→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   470→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/24/deepseek-v4/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">DeepSeek V4 Analysis</a>\n   471→                    </div>\n   472→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   473→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>Chinese AI lab DeepSeek released frontier-level models at lower price points.\n   474→                    </div>\n   475→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   476→                        <span class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</span>\n   477→                    </div>\n   478→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   479→                        <span class=\"topic\">LLM</span>\n   480→                        <span class=\"topic\">open source</span>\n   481→                    </div>\n   482→                </div>\n   483→\n   484→                <div class=\"item\">\n   485→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   486→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/24/openai-gpt-5-5-release/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GPT-5.5 Released</a>\n   487→                    </div>\n   488→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   489→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>OpenAI's \"smartest and most intuitive\" model yet, continuing push toward AI super app.\n   490→                    </div>\n   491→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   492→                        <span class=\"meta-item\">Lucas Ropek</span>\n   493→                    </div>\n   494→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   495→                        <span class=\"topic\">OpenAI</span>\n   496→                        <span class=\"topic\">GPT-5.5</span>\n   497→                    </div>\n   498→                </div>\n   499→\n   500→                <div class=\"item\">\n   501→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   502→                        <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/24/google-anthropic-investment\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Google's $10B Anthropic Investment</a>\n   503→                    </div>\n   504→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   505→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>$10B initially, potential for $30B more. Amazon also invested $5B with potential for $20B more.\n   506→                    </div>\n   507→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   508→                        <span class=\"meta-item\">Jay Peters</span>\n   509→                    </div>\n   510→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   511→                        <span class=\"topic\">Anthropic</span>\n   512→                        <span class=\"topic\">investment</span>\n   513→                    </div>\n   514→                </div>\n   515→\n   516→                <div class=\"item\">\n   517→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   518→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/23/claude-code-quality/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Code Postmortem</a>\n   519→                    </div>\n   520→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   521→                        <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>Quality issues caused by harness bugs, not models. Key bug caused older thinking to be cleared from idle sessions.\n   522→                    </div>\n   523→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   524→                        <span class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</span>\n   525→                    </div>\n   526→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   527→                        <span class=\"topic\">Claude Code</span>\n   528→                        <span class=\"topic\">bugs</span>\n   529→                    </div>\n   530→                </div>\n   531→\n   532→                <div class=\"item\">\n   533→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   534→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/qwen3-6-27b/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Qwen3.6-27B Performance</a>\n   535→                    </div>\n   536→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   537→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>Flagship-level agentic coding in 27B model, surpasses previous 397B MoE. 55.6GB vs 807GB.\n   538→                    </div>\n   539→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   540→                        <span class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</span>\n   541→                    </div>\n   542→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   543→                        <span class=\"topic\">Qwen</span>\n   544→                        <span class=\"topic\">local models</span>\n   545→                    </div>\n   546→                </div>\n   547→\n   548→                <div class=\"item\">\n   549→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   550→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/firefox-mythos/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Firefox 150 + Claude Mythos</a>\n   551→                    </div>\n   552→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   553→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>271 vulnerability fixes from Claude Mythos Preview. \"Every bit as capable\" as top security researchers.\n   554→                    </div>\n   555→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   556→                        <span class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</span>\n   557→                    </div>\n   558→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   559→                        <span class=\"topic\">Claude</span>\n   560→                        <span class=\"topic\">security</span>\n   561→                    </div>\n   562→                </div>\n   563→\n   564→                <div class=\"item\">\n   565→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   566→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/22/github-copilot-pricing/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Copilot Pricing Changes</a>\n   567→                    </div>\n   568→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   569→                        <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>Agentic workflows fundamentally changed compute demands. Long-running parallelized sessions consuming far more resources.\n   570→                    </div>\n   571→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   572→                        <span class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</span>\n   573→                    </div>\n   574→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   575→                        <span class=\"topic\">GitHub Copilot</span>\n   576→                        <span class=\"topic\">pricing</span>\n   577→                    </div>\n   578→                </div>\n   579→\n   580→                <div class=\"item\">\n   581→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   582→                        <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/22/google-ai-generated-code\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Google: 75% AI-Generated Code</a>\n   583→                    </div>\n   584→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   585→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>Up from 50% last fall. Google created \"strike team\" to catch up to Anthropic (70-90% with Claude Code).\n   586→                    </div>\n   587→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   588→                        <span class=\"meta-item\">Stevie Bonifield</span>\n   589→                    </div>\n   590→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   591→                        <span class=\"topic\">Google</span>\n   592→                        <span class=\"topic\">Claude Code</span>\n   593→                    </div>\n   594→                </div>\n   595→\n   596→                <div class=\"item\">\n   597→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   598→                        <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/22/anthropic-mythos-breach\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Anthropic Mythos Breach</a>\n   599→                    </div>\n   600→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   601→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>Unauthorized group gained access to exclusive cyber tool Mythos. Described as \"humiliating\" breach.\n   602→                    </div>\n   603→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   604→                        <span class=\"meta-item\">The Verge</span>\n   605→                    </div>\n   606→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   607→                        <span class=\"topic\">Anthropic</span>\n   608→                        <span class=\"topic\">security</span>\n   609→                    </div>\n   610→                </div>\n   611→\n   612→                <div class=\"item\">\n   613→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   614→                        <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/2026/4/21/spacex-cursor-acquisition\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SpaceX → Cursor $60B</a>\n   615→                    </div>\n   616→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   617→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>SpaceX working with Cursor, option to buy for $60B. Shows massive valuations for AI coding tools.\n   618→                    </div>\n   619→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   620→                        <span class=\"meta-item\">Elizabeth Lopatto</span>\n   621→                    </div>\n   622→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   623→                        <span class=\"topic\">SpaceX</span>\n   624→                        <span class=\"topic\">Cursor</span>\n   625→                    </div>\n   626→                </div>\n   627→\n   628→                <div class=\"item\">\n   629→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   630→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/20/claude-token-counter/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Token Counter Update</a>\n   631→                    </div>\n   632→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   633→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>Opus 4.7 uses new tokenizer. 1.0-1.35x increase, system prompts 1.46x increase. 40% more expensive.\n   634→                    </div>\n   635→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   636→                        <span class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</span>\n   637→                    </div>\n   638→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   639→                        <span class=\"topic\">Claude</span>\n   640→                        <span class=\"topic\">pricing</span>\n   641→                    </div>\n   642→                </div>\n   643→\n   644→                <div class=\"item\">\n   645→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   646→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/19/headless-everything/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Headless Services Future</a>\n   647→                    </div>\n   648→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   649→                        <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>API-first services becoming more common as personal AIs prefer APIs over GUIs. APIs ready for comeback.\n   650→                    </div>\n   651→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   652→                        <span class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</span>\n   653→                    </div>\n   654→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   655→                        <span class=\"topic\">APIs</span>\n   656→                        <span class=\"topic\">AI agents</span>\n   657→                    </div>\n   658→                </div>\n   659→\n   660→                <div class=\"item\">\n   661→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   662→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Apr/18/claude-opus-system-prompts/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Opus System Prompts</a>\n   663→                    </div>\n   664→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   665→                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>Analysis of differences between Claude Opus 4.6 and 4.7 system prompts. Only major lab to publish them.\n   666→                    </div>\n   667→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   668→                        <span class=\"meta-item\">Simon Willison</span>\n   669→                    </div>\n   670→                    <div class=\"topics\">\n   671→                        <span class=\"topic\">Claude</span>\n   672→                        <span class=\"topic\">system prompts</span>\n   673→                    </div>\n   674→                </div>\n   675→            </section>\n   676→        </div>\n   677→    </main>\n   678→\n   679→    <footer class=\"footer\">\n   680→        <p>\n   681→            <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n   682→            <a href=\"#\">Archive</a>\n   683→            <a href=\"#\">RSS Feed</a>\n   684→            <a href=\"#\">Contact</a>\n   685→        </p>\n   686→        <p style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">Generated by AgentDaily Research • 2026-04-25</p>\n   687→    </footer>\n   688→</body>\n   689→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
